				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6846344&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606337834" alt="JamaisJ" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6846344)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;" >JamaisJ</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606320018 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 Nov 2020 16:00</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4827906">
									

<p>Three basic problems:<br />
1) You need to do a little editing; it sounds as if the people being attacked are having their existence erased rather than just apparently the SCP itself. Frankly, that sounds like an interesting anomaly in and of itself; in modern society, those without a paper trail have a number of problems. That also adds a certain level of irony as the aggressors are being punished by being reduced to what they see the victims as, just people with no real identity.</p>
<p>2) This is pretty much just a standard revenge-motivated anomaly. While I'm not saying it's not a worthy cause, it just feels like it's being done more for shock value than for an interesting SCP. Again, it's more because of the violence than anything else; it just lacks something because it's pretty much the usual &quot;commit crime and die&quot; situation.</p>
<p>3) A shape-shifter avenging crimes is not a &quot;vicious and psychotic beast&quot;. It has very specific targets, it's avenging a crime, and it's doing what it can to prevent collateral damage. Passionate, sure, but not necessarily psychotic; just because you can't understand why it's killing doesn't mean it doesn't have valid reasons from its perspective.</p>
<p>You can't apply human psychology to something that may be playing by its own rules.</p>
<p>It may have an almost-physical need to kill sexual assaulters, it may require something from them to live, or it may see them as meat it can target. It may even have a religious reason for doing so. All of which moves it out of the &quot;psychotic&quot; realm.</p>

							</div>

								
					
